# Project context

Use these sources before changing the corresponding area:

- `ARCHITECTURE.md`: system boundaries, entry points, data model, and active design choices.
- `ESTIMATION.md`: estimation formulas and removed designs.
- `DATA_DRIVEN_PROFILES.md`: matcher features, anchors, and similarity behavior.
- `vercel.json`: production routes and cron schedules.
- `backend/src/games/sales-modeling.constants.ts`: numeric estimation constants.
- `backend/src/entities/` and `backend/src/db/migrations/index.ts`: database schema and migration registry.

When documentation and code disagree, treat the code as the current behavior, report the discrepancy, and update both when the requested change affects them.

## Invariants

- The public headline (`estimatedToday`) is the sum of per-platform model estimates.
- Declared milestones are cross-checks; they never floor, cap, or calibrate the model.
- Do not reintroduce per-game calibration, `GenreProfile`, or `pureEstimatedToday`.
- Alinea Analytics / Rhys Elliot milestones are high-value: never soft-reject or junk-clean them as low-trust estimates (see `alinea-milestones` rule).
- Free-to-play games are not estimated.
- Nintendo Switch and mobile estimation are out of scope.
- Schema changes require a TypeORM migration registered explicitly in `backend/src/db/migrations/index.ts`.
- The project has no tests and no test tooling. Do not add tests unless the user explicitly requests tests in the current message. Verify with typecheck, lint, build, or targeted runtime checks instead.

## Workflows

Use the relevant project skill for database access, estimate-divergence diagnosis, catalog discovery, and Vercel cron management. Read the source-of-truth document named by that skill before making changes.

After any code or config change, before reporting done, follow the `sync-skills-and-rules` skill: grep `.cursor/skills` and `.cursor/rules` for what changed and fix stale statements. Ask before changing a rule that encodes user policy.
